{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1179334-weaver-minions","id":1179334,"title":"Weaver Minions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-25T16:20:51-08:00","id":1179334,"title":"Weaver Minions","content":"I was just pondering how it's somewhat strange that the Weaver doesn't have the remotely the same degree of knowing agents in the physical world that the Wyrm does. There are Drones, but they are far from as numerous as Fomori, and don't have the kind of institutional creation or organization that the Fomori do via Pentex - which is especially surprising given that institutional hierarchies are inherently a &quot;Weaverish&quot; element. Similarly there are no Fera splats that serve the Weaver the way the BSDs and the Kumo Spiders serve the Wyrm (at most you get a suspect camp like the Cyberdogs).<br /> <br /> The only &quot;Weaverish&quot; organization comparable to Pentex's vast empire in service of the Wyrm would be the (only reference obliquely in Werewolf materials) Technocratic Union - but assuming you stick to Mage canon there, they are not knowing minions or worshipers in the same way. The tiny minority of Technocrats who know anything about the Weaver (mostly Void Engineers) would see it as a hostile extradimensional entity, not an object of worship or service, even if Technocratic successes correspond with the expansion of its webs in the Umbra. There's DNA, but IIRC they aren't knowing servants the way Pentex is either.<br /> <br /> Do you feel like the setting would be well served by the addition of more active knowing Weaver minions in the physical world, the way the Wyrm is served by Pentex, First Teams, and Black Spiral Dancers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T16:31:26-08:00","id":1179338,"title":"","content":"IIRC, Book of the City discusses Men in Black as being something completely unconnected to the Technocracy and Mage. <br /> <br /> Personally, after Werewolf: The Forsaken came out, I eventually adapted the Ivory Claws into Weaver counterparts to the Black Spiral Dancers. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T16:51:03-08:00","id":1179346,"title":"","content":"The easiest thing to do in a pure Werewolf game would probably just be to recast the Technocrats as knowing Weaver-Namebreakers (since in this scenario we're just using Werewolf cosmology without Mage paradigmatic conflict), and make Men-in-Black Drones they command the same way Pentex uses Fomori.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T16:53:22-08:00","id":1179349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1179334-weaver-minions?p=1179338#post1179338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, after Werewolf: The Forsaken came out, I eventually adapted the Ivory Claws into Weaver counterparts to the Black Spiral Dancers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same ideology of Blood Purity and catharsis through pain, or just using the name with more WtA Weaver-tech themes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T17:03:34-08:00","id":1179354,"title":"","content":"I worked them as a fallen Silver Fang house who are obsessed with blood purity and controlled breeding, strict social order/hierarchy, obedience and group conformity. While they've developed an increasing number of tech-related Gifts over the past century, it's more of a side-effect than their main focus. Mental domination of humans and other &quot;lesser&quot; creatures is another of their specialties, as is finding and exploiting weakness and flaws in others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T18:16:43-08:00","id":1179385,"title":"","content":"My game had the 'One-Song Singers'. They were my version of the Weavers BSD. They are the Cyber Dogs 2.0. After their failure, they continued in secret improving themselves until the spirit of Nanotechnology was born. With its guidance they were able to perfect their cyberneticism to the point they they are no longer bound to one form after their 'ascension'. Kind of transformers beast wars kind of shapeshifting. All of the tribes fetishes are 'upgrades' to their base systems and are basically their version of mutations which do manifest visually just like BSD. They function IC pretty much like the Borg from Star Trek. They don't reproduce, they assimilate. They are never in a group less then 3 which for all intents and purposes is just like a pack.<br /> <br /> Their gifts allowed them to communicate telepathically, gain insight from the pattern webs, create temporary pocket realms, raise the gauntlet, absorb fetishes. Honestly I loved them as antagonists. Even had my players going at the local Glass Walkers for awhile before they figured out it was a third party.<br /> <br /> Edit: Forgot to mention that they also work very closely with Shinzui Enterprise (the Weaver version of Pentex).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","user":"Derzhuzad","date":". 01-25-2018, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T22:06:22-08:00","id":1179438,"title":"","content":"Honestly.. if I were going to take something from the CWOD and backgate it.. The God-Machine and all its bits. Maybe not the Descended but stigmatics, infrastructure, clockwork angels...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T01:20:32-08:00","id":1179459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1179334-weaver-minions?p=1179346#post1179346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The easiest thing to do in a pure Werewolf game would probably just be to recast the Technocrats as knowing Weaver-Namebreakers (since in this scenario we're just using Werewolf cosmology without Mage paradigmatic conflict), and make Men-in-Black Drones they command the same way Pentex uses Fomori.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want something more complex and scary with what is happening in regards to the Technocracy and the Weaver, then you can have Technocrat True Mages who have found a way of arranging and organizing a timed possession by Weaver Spirits of willing Technocrat True Mages. Both the Technocrats who become Drone True Mages for a period of time and those that help organize and hide it care nothing for Weaver's goals - though for some the line between the Weaver's aims and the Technocracy aims has began to blur. (And for some maybe even the line between the Technocracy and the Weaver has began to blur.)<br /> The Technocrats mainly use the possession periods to create and develop Coincidental Inspired Science, which has a tendency to be much less Paradox prone (the trade-off is that they cannot use and develop Vulgar True Magick during this time). Some are used as elite agents at the Front Lines, using the Drone Spirit Gifts as a trump card during a given mission. Others use the possession to enchance their minds during it, becoming extraordinary planners and prediction makers for a time.<br /> <br /> Some have even compared it to what mystic True Mages like the Bata'a do with the so-called spirit-riding. The crucial difference here is that the possession results in a Drone True Mage being created for a time. (That this can be reversed might be because of True Magick Spheres at 6 and more being involved.)<br /> <br /> <br /> I think there is a problem with involving Drones that needs to be resolved: Drones are too strong once they are used outside the narrow roles that they were outlined in in Werewolf books. For example the regeneration, and the Paradox avoidence of Drone True Mages would have to be toned down greatly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-26-2018, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T01:22:22-08:00","id":1179460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1179334-weaver-minions#post1179334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ...and don't have the kind of institutional creation or organization that the Fomori do via Pentex...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's always Wal-Mart -- Er -- I mean, <i>Star</i>Mart...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T03:38:41-08:00","id":1179479,"title":"","content":"You don't need to know about the weaver to serve the weaver. i believe iteration X is supposed to be way too into becoming the machine, and I do have certain glass walkers go too weaver.. The thing is that the wyrm's desperate, the weaver's winning and doesn't need many servants to keep it that way.. Infact, I will go full cyberpunk should anyone go too far along the timeline, complete with hunter spiders walking the streets for reality deviants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T12:17:01-08:00","id":1179567,"title":"","content":"Hmm.<br /> <br /> An education-oriented PAC/lobbyist group advocating for a focus on rote learning, school uniforms, standardized testing, social conformity and equality of outcomes in public schooling.<br /> <br /> An internet watchdog group trying to discredit, block access to, censor and otherwise shut down &quot;undocumented&quot; or &quot;unauthenticated&quot; news sources. <br /> <br /> A data mining company that watches and compiles files on <i>everyone</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}